# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 2d (partner opens 1C).
title: Partner opens 1♣: a strong response
id: L02-16
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.6
student: S
board: 16
dealer: W
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  92     KQ5    KJ74   KQ62
  E  J84    T82    T652   A83
  S  KQT53  AJ4    AQ8    J7
  W  A76    9763   93     T954

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 1S*    = 6+ points, four or more spades
     key: 17 points and five spades. Start by showing your suit. 1♠ is forcing, so partner will bid again.
     not 1NT: 1NT shows 6-9. Did you count 17?
     not 2NT: 2NT shows 12-14 and no suit to show. You have five spades.
     not 3NT: A jump to 3NT isn't in our system. Show your spades first.
     not *: With five spades, which response shows them?
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = A balanced minimum, 13-14, fewer than four spades
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = Game
     key: Partner showed 13-14. With your 17, your side has 30 or more: bid game. Partner has fewer than four spades, so no-trump is the place.
     not Pass: Partner showed 13-14. With your 17, is there enough for game?
     not 2NT: 2NT invites. With 30 points between you, do you need partner's help to decide?
     not 4S: Partner has fewer than four spades. Which game is the better bet?
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Your 1♠ showed spades and 6+ points, and partner has to bid again. His
  1NT showed a balanced 13-14 without four spades. Your 17 makes 30
  between you, so you bid game, in no-trump. North is declarer, because he
  bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E D2  S DQ  W D3  N D4
      note: Dummy's ♦Q wins.
  2   S CJ  W C4  N C2  E CA
      note: Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take diamonds, hearts, clubs and spades. Dummy's ♣J first, the high card from the short side.
  3   E C8  S C7  W C5  N CQ
  4   N S2  E S4  S SK  W S6
      note: A spade to dummy's king.
  5   S H4  W H3  N HQ  E H2
      note: Back to declarer's ♥Q.
  6   N S9  E S8  S SQ  W SA
      note: Another spade, to drive out the ace.
  7   W D9  N D7  E D5  S DA
  8   S HA  W H6  N H5  E H8
      note: The ♥A.
  9   S D8  W H7  N DJ  E D6
      note: Over to declarer's diamonds.
  10  N DK  E DT  S S3  W H9
      note: The ♦K.
  11  N HK  E HT  S HJ  W S7
      note: The ♥K.
  12  N CK  E C3  S S5  W C9
      note: The ♣K.
  13  N C6  E SJ  S ST  W CT
      note: West takes the last trick. 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take four diamonds, three
  hearts, two clubs and at least one spade.

  3NT made with an overtrick. Showing your spades first let partner tell
  you he didn't have four, and you knew no-trump was the game to bid.
